# P3 Test: Replace List.foldl with List.any / List.all

Tests that Catala's `exists` and `for all` collection operations compile
to `List.any` and `List.all` in Lean4 instead of `List.foldl`.

## Before P3 (Lean4 output):

```
-- exists x in collection such that x > 0:
(List.foldl (fun (_acc : Bool) (x : Int) => _acc || (decide (x > 0))) false items)

-- for all x in collection we have x > 0:
(List.foldl (fun (_acc : Bool) (x : Int) => _acc && (decide (x > 0))) true items)
```

## After P3 (Lean4 output):

```
-- exists x in collection such that x > 0:
(List.any items (fun (x : Int) => (decide (x > 0))))

-- for all x in collection we have x > 0:
(List.all items (fun (x : Int) => (decide (x > 0))))
```

```catala
declaration scope CollectionOps:
  input items content list of integer
  output has_positive content boolean
  output all_positive content boolean
  output has_large content boolean

scope CollectionOps:
  definition has_positive equals
    exists item among items such that item > 0

  definition all_positive equals
    for all item among items we have item > 0

  definition has_large equals
    exists item among items such that item > 100
```
